WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.600
And we have breaking

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.168
news, sad breaking news this morning.

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:03.970
Music icon Tony Bennett has died

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:05.605
at the age of 96.

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:07.240
Clem Los joins us now.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.675
And Chloe,

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:10.810
legend feels like an understatement

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:11.578
to some degree

00:00:11.578 --> 00:00:13.813
when you talk about Tony Bennett.

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:16.249
What more can you tell us?

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:18.151
You came along. Yes.

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:19.953
I mean, incredibly sad news

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:21.421
for people all over the world

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:22.055
this morning.

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:25.091
Tony Bennett has died at the age of 96.

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:27.060
His publicist, Sylvia Weiner,

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.062
his longtime publicist

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:30.530
confirming this morning.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:33.867
And this comes as a shock to many.

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:36.836
He lived a long, beautiful life.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.571
I had the honor of meeting him

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:39.773
when he turns 90

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:40.940
and performed in New York

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.475
at the Rainbow Room.

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:44.377
We don't know the circumstances

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:45.412
of his death,

00:00:45.412 --> 00:00:46.479
but we know that he had been

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:47.847
battling Alzheimer's

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:49.382
for the past several years.

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:50.683
His wife, Susan Bennett,

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:54.587
she actually told AARP magazine in 20, 21

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:57.524
that despite the Alzheimer's,

00:00:57.524 --> 00:00:59.659
he was continuing to perform

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:01.995
put out music.

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:03.696
Obviously we know that he toured

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:05.432
and put out albums with Lady Gaga.

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:06.800
I've reached out to her

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.468
and I'm sure that this is obviously

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:10.437
a devastating loss for her.

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:12.639
They were just so close.

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:16.209
But his career spanned decades

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:16.843
from the early

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:19.179
1950s and Frank Sinatra

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:20.647
is someone who touted him

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:22.682
as one of the greatest voices

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:24.451
of a generation.

00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:27.587
And so I meeting Tony Bennett

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:29.823
there's just nothing like like it.

00:01:30.657 --> 00:01:33.493
And he was so charismatic, so kind

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:36.362
and just obviously so talented.

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:39.099
And so it's a very sad day.

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:40.600
For everyone

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:42.102
who had the pleasure of meeting

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:42.769
him, knowing him,

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:44.437
or just loving his music, to know

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:45.939
that he has passed

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:48.708
at his home in New York at the age of 96

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:49.742
Yeah.

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:50.643
And this is a

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:52.178
this is a legend, really,

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:53.746
whose career spans

00:01:53.746 --> 00:01:55.115
many, many decades,

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:57.617
going all the way back to the 1950s.

00:01:57.617 --> 00:01:58.384
And as you were talking

00:01:58.384 --> 00:01:59.586
Chloe, we were playing

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:01.921
some of that video of Tony Bennett

00:02:02.088 --> 00:02:03.123
as he was making one

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:04.557
of his last performances,

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:06.826
maybe even the last, with Lady Gaga.

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:10.797
He was able to, even in his final years

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:13.233
as he was battling Alzheimer's, still

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:15.301
perform and

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:18.838
really give the audience

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:20.640
what they've always loved about him,

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:23.576
which is his ability to perform music.

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:24.377
And Lady Gaga

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:25.879
really kind of identified with him,

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:28.948
bringing him in to this modern era.

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:30.750
We actually have with us now

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.119
Anderson Cooper on the phone.

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:35.388
Anderson, you've spent some time

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:36.823
with Tony Bennett.

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:38.758
What are you thinking about today

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:40.627
as we mark his passing?

00:02:40.627 --> 00:02:41.828
Well, it just

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:43.329
I mean, what an extraordinary life.

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:45.031
I had the honor of

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:46.699
doing a profile of Tony

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:48.468
and his wife Susan.

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:51.037
And for 60 minutes

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:52.205
when he did

00:02:52.205 --> 00:02:53.907
his final shows with Lady Gaga

00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:55.175
that you were just talking about.

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:56.576
And I got to spend

00:02:56.576 --> 00:02:58.011
a significant amount of time with him.

00:02:58.011 --> 00:02:59.712
I was in his apartment

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:01.347
watching him rehearse

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:03.216
with his longtime accompanist.

00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:04.551
You know,

00:03:04.551 --> 00:03:06.619
he has lived just an extraordinary

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:07.287
epic life.

00:03:07.287 --> 00:03:07.887
There's a lot of people

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:08.221
who don't know

00:03:08.221 --> 00:03:09.856
a lot of the details of his life

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:13.126
and in his service during

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:14.093
the service of the country

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:15.628
during the war.

00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:18.031
He was one of the early artists involved

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:20.266
in the civil rights movement

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:21.634
in a very serious way.

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:24.871
Marching is performing.

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:27.106
He sacrificed a lot

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:29.409
over the years for that.

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:31.244
But, you know,

00:03:31.244 --> 00:03:33.346
I think his most extraordinary

00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:35.315
performances are in

00:03:35.315 --> 00:03:36.683
the last three performances

00:03:36.683 --> 00:03:38.384
that he did at Radio City with Lady Gaga.

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:40.386
I think everybody who was there

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:43.356
knew that they were witnessing

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:45.325
something really just incredible

00:03:45.325 --> 00:03:47.760
that this man who

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.996
much of his memory was gone.

00:03:49.996 --> 00:03:52.432
He when I was interviewing him,

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:53.499
I would be talking to him.

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:54.634
And he

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:55.134
you know,

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:57.136
he would not remember

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:58.171
what he had just said.

00:03:58.171 --> 00:03:59.472
He would not remember certainly

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:01.441
who I was sitting there talking to him.

00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:04.944
But his wife, Susan, all during COVID,

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:08.815
kept him engaged kept him

00:04:08.815 --> 00:04:10.950
kept him alive and kept him, Tony.

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:12.552
And in the end,

00:04:12.552 --> 00:04:13.219
Tony Bennett

00:04:13.219 --> 00:04:14.787
knew who Tony Bennett was

00:04:14.787 --> 00:04:18.091
when when Alzheimer's had had robbed him

00:04:18.224 --> 00:04:20.526
of many of his plays,

00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:22.428
of his extraordinary life.

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:25.832
He knew inherently in in his mind,

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:27.500
still that he was Tony Bennett.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:29.535
And when that music started to play,

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:33.506
he would you could see him

00:04:34.207 --> 00:04:36.175
transforming into Tony Bennett

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:37.210
once again.

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:38.444
And I said

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:39.212
I stood there

00:04:39.212 --> 00:04:40.513
by the piano in his apartment

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:42.415
while he's rehearsing his.

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:43.750
And I just interviewed him.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:44.317
And it had been

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:45.151
a very difficult interview

00:04:45.151 --> 00:04:46.152
because you could only say

00:04:46.152 --> 00:04:49.055
a few sentences and clearly didn't

00:04:49.722 --> 00:04:52.592
really know why we were there.

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:54.594
But as soon as his piano player

00:04:54.594 --> 00:04:56.929
started playing a few bars,

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:58.931
he trotted up to the piano with this

00:04:59.499 --> 00:05:01.701
this incredible energy,

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:03.436
put his elbow on the piano,

00:05:03.436 --> 00:05:05.972
and he just launched into an hour

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:08.207
long set of all his greatest hits

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:10.043
without any sheet music, nothing.

00:05:10.043 --> 00:05:12.211
It was all from memory and it was all so,

00:05:12.578 --> 00:05:14.013
you know, and it just

00:05:14.013 --> 00:05:14.814
it was one of the most

00:05:14.814 --> 00:05:16.015
extraordinary experience in my life

00:05:16.015 --> 00:05:17.917
to stand there and watch it.

00:05:17.917 --> 00:05:20.320
And suddenly, while he was singing,

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:21.154
because I was standing

00:05:21.154 --> 00:05:22.322
by the piano with him,

00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:23.489
he was looking at me

00:05:23.489 --> 00:05:25.925
and relating to me as Tony Bennett.

00:05:25.992 --> 00:05:28.461
And if I didn't know better,

00:05:28.461 --> 00:05:29.162
I would have thought

00:05:29.162 --> 00:05:30.630
he knew exactly who I was

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:31.597
or why I was there.

00:05:31.597 --> 00:05:33.766
And engaging with it,

00:05:33.833 --> 00:05:34.901
he was engaging with me

00:05:34.901 --> 00:05:36.602
in a way through the music

00:05:36.602 --> 00:05:38.871
that he couldn't do in any other way. So

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:41.741
it's such a it's a sad day.

00:05:41.741 --> 00:05:42.975
Of course,

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:43.876
you know,

00:05:43.876 --> 00:05:45.912
we've all lost one of the great artists

00:05:45.912 --> 00:05:47.880
of our time, and yet

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.182
what a triumphant life.

00:05:49.182 --> 00:05:51.718
And to have sent this,

00:05:52.018 --> 00:05:52.385
you know,

00:05:52.385 --> 00:05:52.952
the message

00:05:52.952 --> 00:05:53.853
that he sent

00:05:53.853 --> 00:05:55.321
to so many families out there

00:05:55.321 --> 00:05:56.556
who are people with loved ones

00:05:56.556 --> 00:05:58.291
with Alzheimer's,

00:05:58.958 --> 00:05:59.258
you know,

00:05:59.258 --> 00:06:00.360
this message of hope

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:03.062
and this message of possibility

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:05.965
that he could still have a

00:06:05.965 --> 00:06:07.433
vibrant life

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:09.535
because of the love of his wife, Susan.

00:06:09.836 --> 00:06:12.438
His son Danny always, always cared

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:15.241
and I'll never forget

00:06:15.241 --> 00:06:16.376
the last performance

00:06:16.376 --> 00:06:17.543
that I had the privilege

00:06:17.543 --> 00:06:18.578
of being at backstage

00:06:18.578 --> 00:06:20.313
with him at Radio City Music Hall

00:06:20.313 --> 00:06:22.382
just a short time before he went on.

00:06:22.949 --> 00:06:24.917
He was in the back and he turned to Susan

00:06:24.917 --> 00:06:27.086
and he didn't know exactly where he was.

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:29.222
And he said, you know, what do we do?

00:06:29.222 --> 00:06:30.590
And she said,

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:31.290
you know, you're

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:32.825
you're performing tonight

00:06:32.825 --> 00:06:34.327
in like 10 minutes.

00:06:34.327 --> 00:06:35.762
And he said, Great.

00:06:35.762 --> 00:06:37.497
And she said, let's go over the set.

00:06:37.497 --> 00:06:38.598
And he said, Great.

00:06:38.598 --> 00:06:39.132
And she did.

00:06:39.132 --> 00:06:40.233
They went over what number

00:06:40.233 --> 00:06:41.467
he was going to do.

00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:42.101
He went back.

00:06:42.101 --> 00:06:43.469
He went to stand in the wings.

00:06:43.469 --> 00:06:45.304
I was standing there with him.

00:06:45.304 --> 00:06:46.973
And as soon as he was watching

00:06:46.973 --> 00:06:48.574
Lady Gaga perform on stage,

00:06:48.574 --> 00:06:49.609
because she was

00:06:49.609 --> 00:06:51.144
he did a set and she did a set.

00:06:51.144 --> 00:06:53.012
And then he would come out at the end

00:06:53.012 --> 00:06:55.014
and she would come out at a certain point

00:06:55.014 --> 00:06:55.882
with him.

00:06:55.882 --> 00:06:57.150
And watching Lady Gaga,

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:58.651
you could see like the music

00:06:58.651 --> 00:06:59.852
just flowing into him.

00:06:59.852 --> 00:07:00.253
And he started

00:07:00.253 --> 00:07:01.087
tapping his feet

00:07:01.087 --> 00:07:03.756
and cooking his fingers together.

00:07:04.123 --> 00:07:06.259
He went out. He killed it out there.

00:07:06.692 --> 00:07:08.161
He went out there with his first words

00:07:08.161 --> 00:07:09.729
with like the crowd just erupted.

00:07:09.729 --> 00:07:11.564
His first words were, wow.

00:07:11.564 --> 00:07:12.932
And they just loved it.

00:07:12.932 --> 00:07:14.066
He did his whole set.

00:07:14.066 --> 00:07:15.067
And then

00:07:15.368 --> 00:07:16.269
the first night

00:07:16.269 --> 00:07:18.304
when Lady Gaga had come out,

00:07:18.304 --> 00:07:20.540
he had said like, wow, look who's here.

00:07:20.573 --> 00:07:22.542
But he hadn't said her name.

00:07:22.542 --> 00:07:22.975
And I

00:07:22.975 --> 00:07:24.644
talked to Lady Gaga about it afterward.

00:07:24.644 --> 00:07:26.112
And she felt that

00:07:26.112 --> 00:07:28.147
he in the moment on the stage,

00:07:28.147 --> 00:07:29.081
those first two nights,

00:07:29.081 --> 00:07:31.184
he didn't remember her name,

00:07:31.184 --> 00:07:33.686
but and while they were rehearsing

00:07:33.686 --> 00:07:34.921
in the weeks leading up to it,

00:07:34.921 --> 00:07:35.822
she was concerned

00:07:35.822 --> 00:07:37.390
that he didn't remember her name.

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:38.491
But on that final night

00:07:38.491 --> 00:07:40.159
when she came out and he turned

00:07:40.159 --> 00:07:41.861
and he saw her coming out

00:07:41.861 --> 00:07:44.730
he said, wow, Lady Gaga.

00:07:45.031 --> 00:07:46.766
And she burst into tears.

00:07:46.766 --> 00:07:48.601
I mean, everybody just burst into tears.

00:07:48.601 --> 00:07:50.770
It was just an extraordinary night. And

00:07:52.171 --> 00:07:52.872
I mean,

00:07:53.072 --> 00:07:55.241
what what a life we have been able to

00:07:55.508 --> 00:07:56.442
to witness

00:07:56.442 --> 00:07:58.444
and benefit from over all these decades.

00:07:59.712 --> 00:08:01.681
Anderson, CNN has now confirmed

00:08:01.681 --> 00:08:02.882
that Tony Bennett has died.

00:08:02.882 --> 00:08:04.650
We're expecting a statement shortly.

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:06.052
The 60 piece that you did,

00:08:06.052 --> 00:08:07.620
Anderson, was so incredibly poignant.

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:09.055
And I remember when,

00:08:09.055 --> 00:08:09.255
you know,

00:08:09.255 --> 00:08:10.957
Lady Gaga was kind of describing that,

00:08:10.957 --> 00:08:12.391
like it was almost like a switch flipped

00:08:12.391 --> 00:08:14.026
and then you demonstrated it.

00:08:14.026 --> 00:08:15.027
We also made a great point.

00:08:15.027 --> 00:08:15.761
The life lived.

00:08:15.761 --> 00:08:16.462
We've only got about a minute

00:08:16.462 --> 00:08:17.430
and a half left.

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:19.265
Civil rights in particular, obviously,

00:08:19.265 --> 00:08:20.600
his military service

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:23.936
Can you capture what what he was

00:08:24.437 --> 00:08:25.605
not just those last performances,

00:08:25.605 --> 00:08:27.773
but just overall.

00:08:28.174 --> 00:08:28.975
This was a kid

00:08:28.975 --> 00:08:30.409
who, you know, didn't have much

00:08:30.409 --> 00:08:33.279
when he was born and had a family that

00:08:33.980 --> 00:08:37.016
loved him and that supported him.

00:08:37.049 --> 00:08:42.522
But he he created who he was and he

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:44.757
he was

00:08:44.757 --> 00:08:45.925
all about music

00:08:45.925 --> 00:08:47.894
from the beginning to the end.

00:08:47.894 --> 00:08:49.262
And, you know,

00:08:49.262 --> 00:08:49.629
his son,

00:08:49.629 --> 00:08:51.931
Danny was incredible manager for him.

00:08:53.299 --> 00:08:54.267
You know, reinterred

00:08:54.267 --> 00:08:55.801
duced him to whole new generations

00:08:55.801 --> 00:08:56.502
of people

00:08:56.502 --> 00:08:57.270
over the decades

00:08:57.270 --> 00:08:58.204
in the 1980s,

00:08:58.204 --> 00:08:59.472
in the 1990s,

00:08:59.472 --> 00:09:00.139
doing duets

00:09:00.139 --> 00:09:00.840
with some of the greatest

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:02.408
contemporary artists of the day.

00:09:02.408 --> 00:09:03.209
And his

00:09:03.209 --> 00:09:04.310
you can't talk about Tony Bennett

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:06.546
without talking about Susan, his wife,

00:09:06.546 --> 00:09:09.482
who loved him her entire life, basically

00:09:09.482 --> 00:09:11.350
grew up listening to his music

00:09:11.350 --> 00:09:11.851
and was

00:09:11.851 --> 00:09:13.052
just an incredible,

00:09:13.052 --> 00:09:15.888
incredible champion and

00:09:15.888 --> 00:09:17.523
partner in all of this.

00:09:17.523 --> 00:09:18.791
And my thoughts

00:09:18.791 --> 00:09:21.093
are certainly with his family today

00:09:21.093 --> 00:09:21.827
and with Tony.

00:09:21.827 --> 00:09:24.163
And, you know,

00:09:24.497 --> 00:09:25.531
there's

00:09:26.032 --> 00:09:26.465
you know,

00:09:26.465 --> 00:09:29.001
